  "worked_solution": "Recall that $\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x=5\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\text{arctan}(5)=1.373\\,400\u2026\u22481.373\\,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $1.373\\,4$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=1.373\\,4.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}=\\pi +{x}_{1}=\\pi +1.373\\,4=4.515\\,0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ is\n\n$$\n1.373\\,4\\cdot 4.515\\,0\u22486.2\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place.",
